    "body": "> Any reason to introduce `sstream` when `printf` is used everywhere else?\r\n\r\nIf you mean instead of using `snprintf`, `sstream` simplifies not needing to manage a local buffer. `testRun->errorMsg` is a `std::string` anyway, so the heap is being allocated no matter what. `ss.str()` is an rvalue, so it should use the move constructor to avoid copy overhead.",
